{"id": "en_story_koepcke", "tag": "TRUE STORY", "cta": "MORE TRUE STORIES LIKE THIS", "ctaSmall": "follow", "ctaWhere": "new story every day", "accent": "#3DDC84", "lang": "en", "total": 71.225, "segments": [{"text": "A 17 year old girl plummets 3,000 m from the sky directly into a dense rainforest.", "start": 0.0, "end": 5.1}, {"text": "On 24 December 1971, lightning strikes LANSA Flight 508 high over the remote Peruvian rainforest.", "start": 5.76, "end": 11.32}, {"text": "The commercial airplane suddenly breaks apart midair and throws passengers into the violent storm below.", "start": 11.84, "end": 16.78}, {"text": "Juliane Koepcke remains strapped tight to her seat row as she falls through empty air.", "start": 16.490000000000002, "end": 21.34}, {"text": "She wakes up completely alone on the ground with a broken collarbone and a concussion.", "start": 21.9, "end": 25.44}, {"text": "Juliane also endures an eye injury along with a painful deep cut on her arm.", "start": 25.110000000000003, "end": 29.8}, {"text": "Her father is a biologist who taught her that following water always leads to people.", "start": 30.38, "end": 34.0}, {"text": "She finds a small creek and begins walking downstream through the dense, dangerous green jungle.", "start": 34.36, "end": 38.92}, {"text": "The creek leads directly into a river, but her painful journey continues without any food.", "start": 39.58, "end": 43.88}, {"text": "After 9 days of steadily following the water, she finally discovers an empty lumberjack camp.", "start": 44.48, "end": 48.86}, {"text": "She waits inside the shelter until local workers discover her after 11 days completely alone.", "start": 49.38, "end": 54.24}, {"text": "Up to 14 others survive the crash, but they all die before help can arrive.", "start": 54.78, "end": 58.34}, {"text": "Juliane emerges as the only living survivor from the terrifying wreckage of the doomed flight.", "start": 58.089999999999996, "end": 63.32}, {"text": "Could you survive 11 d